I close my computer.
The video call with my family is over.
I smile and look around the living room.
It is warm and cozy here.
Many things are different now.
I think about my first days in Denmark.
January was a very cold month.
The first weeks were a big challenge.
I missed my family a lot.
Everything in the city was new to me.
My neighbour Nina welcomed me.
Now I have a soft sofa and a nice rug.
I take the bus to work every morning.
I talk with Peter and the other colleagues.
The winter was long.
But I learned a lot in the first months.
I am no longer just a guest in the city.
I look out of the window.
I drink the rest of my tea, and I am happy.
I feel completely at home.
